      "content": "Focus on vocabulary that is overly precise, abstract, or conspicuously formal when the topic doesn't demand it. Look for elevated nominalizations—turning verbs into nouns (e.g., \"implementation\" instead of \"implementing\")—which distance the language from human action. Furthermore, watch for passive constructions, as they obscure the true agent or actor, making the message feel impersonal and controlled.",
